+# SB-55 application integration still required
+
+The ChromiumEngine methods are already wired; they are not the product UI.
+Promote them to a BrowserEngine capability with safe WebKit no-op defaults.
+
+Settings: per-profile “Automatically show videos and calls in picture-in-picture”
+toggle, initially reflecting autoPictureInPictureEnabled(profile). Each edit calls
+setAutoPictureInPictureEnabled(profile, enabled:). Off overrides site allows.
+Site Controls: Automatic PiP choice Default / Allow / Block; call
+setAutoPictureInPictureException(profile, origin: origin, enabled: nil/true/false).
+Keep the displayed exceptions in the app's profile settings model. Engine content
+settings persist the effective rules. Do not treat page paths as separate sites.
+
+On tab/Space switch retain the existing detach/attach calls. After attaching, set
+setPictureInPictureWindowActive(tab, active: hostWindow.isKeyWindow). Send false
+to the selected tab when its host resigns key; true when it becomes key again.
+Do not send “active” simply because a tab was attached in a background window.
+Do not create another Browser or fake a user gesture to trigger PiP.
+
+Subscribe to pictureInPictureDidChange to track the owning EngineTab. Subscribe
+to pictureInPictureRequestsTab to select its model's window, Space, then tab and
+focus its page. Chromium already draws a return-to-tab button for video and
+Document PiP. If a platform/UI variant lacks it, draw a Back to tab control tied
+to the same model action. Closing PiP alone must not be treated as leaving a call.
+
+Placement is engine-owned, default bottom-right with a 20 point margin. Drag and
+resize persist per profile. Optional “Reset PiP position” calls
+setPictureInPictureFrame(profile, frame: .zero). Do not reposition to top-right.
+
+Site-provided Document PiP owns mute/camera/leave controls and track state.
+Fallback camera-tile UI for sites without Document PiP is not implemented.
+No application UI or native window switching is qualified by this patch.
